 34CL c  {+36}Ar|)1p+1n+{+34}Cl from J|p=0+ {+36}Ar ground state.               
 34CL c  1969Br21: a 45-MeV deuteron beam was produced from the Berkeley 88-Inch
 34CL2c  Cyclotron. The target was 99.6%-enriched {+36}Ar gas. Reaction products
 34CL3c  were detected using a 155-|mm phosphorus-diffused silicon |DE          
 34CL4c  transmission counter and a 3.0-mm lithium-drifted silicon E counter    
 34CL5c  operated in coincidence, followed by a 0.5-mm lithium-drifted silicon  
 34CL6c  E-reject counter operated in anti-coincidence with the first two       
 34CL7c  counters to eliminate long-range particles. Measured |s(E{-|a},|q).    
 34CL8c  Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, |p, and isospin. Also measured         
 34CL9c  {+36}Ar(p,t){+34}Ar and {+36}Ar(p,{+3}He){+34}Cl.                      
 34CL c  1972Ho02: a 19-MeV deuteron beam bombarded a 99.6%-enriched {+36}Ar gas
 34CL2c  target. Outgoing |a particles were momentum-analyzed by the Enge       
 34CL3c  split-pole spectrograph and detected in 100-|mm Ilford K0 nuclear      
 34CL4c  emulsion plates. Measured |s(E{-|a},|q). Deduced levels, L-transfers,  
 34CL5c  J, |p, and isospin from DWUCK-DWBA analysis.                           
 34CL c  1982Ta04 (supersedes 1980To13: {+36}Ar(pol d,|a) E=16 MeV.             
 34CL2c  99.9%-enriched target. Used four solid-state detectors of 100-200 keV  
 34CL3c  FWHM and did analyzing power measurements. Did DWBA analysis (code     
 34CL4c  DWUCK)                                                                 
 35CL c  Others: Measured cross section of {+36}Ar(d,|a){+34m}Cl, E|<8.4 MeV    
 35CL2c  (2011En01,2012En01)                                                    
